SUMMARY:'Photo Diary' Exhibition - Karolina Kuras & Ted Belton
DESCRIPTION:On May 2026\, Album Studios (@album.studios ) and CONTACT Photography Festival (@contactphoto) unveil the works of internationally renowned ballet and fashion photographers\, Karolina Kuras (@karolinakuras) and Ted Belton (@tedbelton) in “Photo Diary”. \nThis 25-day exhibition brings together an intimate record of Kuras’ and Belton’s photography practices\, capturing discipline and grace in visual conversation. Both with special eyes for movement\, texture\, and contrast\, their photographs reveal how fashion and dance are connected practices\, through their vulnerable yet performative natures. \nThe presentation features curated photographs\, unified by a sense of experimentation with human expression\, varied creative processes\, and print materials. Central to the exhibition is the artists’ contemporary styles that naturally complement each other\, capturing discipline and grace in visual conversation. \nThe evening will include the artists in attendance and a panel moderated by Odessa Paloma Parker (@odessapaloma). Light refreshments will be provided. Photobooth hosted by Album EQ (@albumequipment) in Studio B. \nAdmission is free. Please RSVP via event website here.  \nAbout the Artists:Karolina Kuras is a Toronto based ballet and portrait photographer. Internationally recognized as one of the foremost photographers working in ballet today\, she works at the intersection of classical ballet and fashion\, producing images that are precise\, elegant\, and entirely her own. A classically trained dancer herself\, Karolina brings an embodied understanding of movement and line to every shoot. On set she directs and shapes movement specifically for the camera\, ensuring each image is intentional rather than incidental. Having worked with some of the most celebrated ballet companies in the world\, her work is built on the trust of the people she photographs and a deep respect and understanding for the art form. \nTed Belton is a Canadian photographer living in Toronto and working internationally. His fashion pictures and portraits have appeared in titles such as AirMail\, Dazed\, Kinfolk\, and Rolling Stone. Ted’s interest in documenting individuals of exceptional character and style has brought him to the streets of Paris\, into the homes of eccentrics and socialites\, the studios of artists\, musicians\, and designers\, and to skate parks and fashion weeks around the world. Wherever he is\, Ted’s eye remains tuned to the quiet qualities of his subjects that he aims to amplify into memorable statements. \nAbout the Moderator:Odessa Paloma Parker is an award-winning writer\, editor\, stylist\, educator and brand strategist based in Toronto. She is the Art Editor at The Globe and Mail Style Magazine\, and in 2022\, she founded Opaloma\, an arts\, culture and style platform featuring stories from Toronto and beyond. Odessa is a co-author of the first edition of Louis Vuitton’s City Guide Toronto\, and her journalistic expertise has been acknowledged by a National Magazine Award nomination. Odessa is also an occasional DJ; her event clients include Chanel\, Bata Shoe Museum and the Art Gallery of Ontario. \nAbout the Venue:Album Studios is a Toronto-based studio rental space for photographers\, film production\, and events. We offer 7 studio spaces across three locations in West Toronto. Namely\, Geary Avenue\, the Junction\, and the Mount Dennis neighbourhoods \nExhibition Details:Title: Photo DiaryArtists: Karolina Kuras and Ted BeltonDates: May 7 – May 31\, 2026Location: Album StudiosAddress:  92 Geary Ave\, TorontoOpening Reception: Thurs\, May 7\, 2026 / 6:00 – 11:00 PM / Refreshments will be served.Gallery Viewing: Fri\, May 8 until Sun\, May 31 / 9:00 AM – 5:00 PM \nEvent Registration: https://luma.com/se9yuygdContact: https://www.albumstudios.com/home 
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/photo-diary-exhibition-karolina-kuras-ted-belton/
LOCATION:Album Studios: Geary\, 92 Geary Ave\, Toronto\, ON M6H 2B6\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6H 2B6
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions,Festivals,Film & Media
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/photo-diary-exhibition-karolina-kuras-ted-belton.png
END:VEVENT
