SUMMARY:In the Light of the Machine: Toward a Relational Ethics of AI
DESCRIPTION:In the Light of the Machine: Toward a Relational Ethics of Artificial Intelligence \nFriday\, May 8\, from 12:00 to 2:00 p.m. \nOnline \nAs AI systems become increasingly entangled with our cultural\, economic\, and ecological worlds\, how do we negotiate an ethical landscape of emergent intelligence? Moving beyond familiar debates over risk and safety\, this conversation brings together panelists who will explore how art can help us sense\, critique\, and reimagine the systems shaping our technological present. By situating AI within broader epistemological and cultural contexts. Moderated by Lisa Deanne Smith\, this panel seeks to expand AI discourse and understand machine learning as a site of relation. \nIn the Light of the Machine: Toward a Relational Ethics of Artificial Intelligence coincides with Onsite Gallery’s current exhibition Becoming (in the light of the miracle) guest curated by Farah Yusuf. \nAlso on view at Onsite Gallery are The Delaney Family Emerging Curator’s Prize: Metabolic Loop and Diego Santamaría (HIDROCK) | The Shared Flight (2025) \nBecoming (in the light of the miracle) is on view at Onsite Gallery until May 16\, 2026 \nBecoming (in the light of the miracle) is generously supported by the Ontario Arts Council\, an agency of the Government of Ontario through the Curatorial Projects: Indigenous and Culturally Diverse program. \nOnsite Gallery is generously supported by The Delaney Family
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/in-the-light-of-the-machine-toward-a-relational-ethics-of-ai/
LOCATION:Onsite Gallery\, 199 Richmond St W Ground Floor\, Toronto\, ON M5V 0H4\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5V 0H4
CATEGORIES:Talks & Panels
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/in-the-light-of-the-machine-toward-a-relational-ethics-of-ai.png
END:VEVENT
