SUMMARY:Adventure Alley - Children's Mental Health Week: Talk & Play
DESCRIPTION:In honour of Children’s Mental Health Week and in collaboration with our current Play with Purpose partner\, George Hull Centre\, we will be hosting our first ever Talk & Play session\, this Friday\, May 8th from 3-5 PM. \nA practical\, play-based session for parents and caregivers on how everyday interactions can support children’s emotional development and sense of belonging—led by a clinical expert(s) in early childhood mental health. Topics will include: \n\nWhy the Early Years Matter: Building Strong Foundations Through PlayPlay isn’t just fun—it’s how young children build the foundation for lifelong mental health.\nUnderstanding Big Feelings in Little KidsWhat looks like behaviour is often communication—learn how to respond in ways that help children thrive\nCreating Environments Where Every Child Can Belong and SucceedEvery child deserves to feel capable\, included\, and supported—here’s how we create that through play and community\n\nEVENT DETAILS: \n\nFriday\, May 8th\n3-5 PM\n3 to 3:30 PM – Talk\n3:30 to 4 PM – Snacks & beverages offered\n4 to 5 PM – Free play\n\nTo celebrate Children’s Mental Health Week\, we’ll be offering 50% off all WALK-IN visits on May 8th! \n\nJoin us for a full day of play\, connection\, and community!\n50% off all visits\nWALK-IN ONLY\n\nABOUT GEORGE HULL CENTRE \nAs a leader in children’s mental health\, the George Hull Centre provides a comprehensive “Circle of Care” for infants\, children\, and pre-teens. They understand that mental health is the foundation of a child’s well-being and will be bringing their expertise\, insights\, and passion to our space! Learn more about our current Play With Purpose partner by clicking HERE.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/adventure-alley-childrens-mental-health-week-talk-play/
LOCATION:Adventure Alley Toronto\, 140 Galleria Rd Unit #2\, Toronto\, ON M6H 2A4\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6H 2A4
CATEGORIES:Classes & Workshops,Community Events,Kids & Family,Talks & Panels
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/adventure-alley-childrens-mental-health-week-talk-play.png
END:VEVENT
